--TEST--
`Core\Router::url` refuses a literal `$params` value outside the closed set its parameter declares, for a path capture and for a `#[Query]` alike — `rule:routing/a-query-parameter-is-declared-like-a-capture` and `rule:routing/a-capture-narrows-to-a-closed-set`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The bound named on both sides in one file: the accepted spelling and the
// first refused one are written at adjacent call sites, and only the second is
// in the error list below. The accepted half is asserted for its *output* in
// `core/router-url-builds-every-value-of-a-captures-closed-set.nvst`, which is
// the half a program that does not compile cannot show.
class Docs {
    // § 5's example, plus § 3's `#[Query]`, which declares the same type list a
    // capture does — so it has a closed set for exactly the same reason.
    // `rule:attributes/access-is-a-required-sibling`: the decision is a required sibling of every `#[Route]`.
    #[Core\Route(path: "/{lang}/docs/{page}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "docs.show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show("en"|"de"|"fr" $lang, string $page, #[Core\Query] "asc"|"desc" $order): string {
        return $lang . "/" . $page . "/" . $order;
    }
}

// The last accepted: the union's final member, and a `$page` whose type names
// no set at all, so nothing about it is checked.
echo Core\Router::url("docs.show", ["lang" => "fr", "page" => "intro"]), "\n";

// The first refused: a segment § 5 says the router answers `404` to, which
// makes this a link to a route that will not match.
echo Core\Router::url("docs.show", ["lang" => "xx", "page" => "intro"]), "\n";

// The same refusal on the query half, where the dead link is the handler's own
// `400` (§ 3) rather than a `404`. One diagnostic per call, not per entry:
// `$params` written against the wrong route is usually wrong in every entry.
echo Core\Router::url("docs.show", ["lang" => "en", "page" => "intro", "order" => "up"]), "\n";

// A *computed* value is not read at all, exactly as a computed key is not:
// there is nothing at the call site to compare against the set.
var $lang = "xx";
echo Core\Router::url("docs.show", ["lang" => $lang, "page" => "intro"]), "\n";

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0772]: `Docs::show` admits `en`, `de`, `fr` for `lang`, and this link supplies `xx`
   --> case.nvs:24:6
%A
error[E0772]: `Docs::show` admits `asc`, `desc` for `order`, and this link supplies `up`
   --> case.nvs:29:6
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
